WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.386
TENET5 presents: A story of accountability.

00:00:03.386 --> 00:00:09.840
This is a guide for younger audiences about how government spending actually works — and what happens when no one is watching the money.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.204
The Messy Treasury.

00:00:11.204 --> 00:00:16.670
The government collects money from everyone — taxes from working people, businesses, imports.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.238
That money goes into a big treasure chest called the federal treasury.

00:00:20.238 --> 00:00:22.284
And a lot of it... goes missing.

00:00:22.284 --> 00:00:23.806
The Broken Piggy Bank.

00:00:23.806 --> 00:00:27.511
The Phoenix Pay System was supposed to replace an old payroll system.

00:00:27.511 --> 00:00:30.215
It cost seven point five billion dollars.

00:00:30.215 --> 00:00:31.215
It didn't work.

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:34.124
Government employees went months without paychecks.

00:00:34.124 --> 00:00:35.499
Some were overpaid.

00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:37.136
Some lost their homes.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.852
The system is still broken.

00:00:38.852 --> 00:00:41.420
The Hungry App. ArriveCAN was a border app.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.965
It was supposed to cost eighty thousand dollars.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:48.022
The Auditor General found it actually cost fifty-nine point five million.

00:00:48.022 --> 00:00:50.738
The people who built it couldn't explain where the money went.

00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:52.272
The Pig Farm Monster.

00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:55.307
Robert Pickton operated a pig farm in Vancouver.

00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:57.749
He confessed to killing forty-nine women.

00:00:57.749 --> 00:01:00.397
Two thousand people attended parties at his farm.

00:01:00.397 --> 00:01:02.295
The Hells Angels were connected.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:06.545
A woman escaped the farm in 1997 and reported to police.

00:01:06.545 --> 00:01:07.977
The charges were dropped.

00:01:07.977 --> 00:01:09.284
Why does this matter?

00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:11.420
Because the police knew for years.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:18.344
They did not investigate because the victims were marginalized — sex workers, Indigenous women, people no one in power thought were important.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:22.374
The Missing Women Commission found systemic failure rooted in who the victims were.

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:23.795
Keep asking questions.

00:01:23.795 --> 00:01:27.181
When someone says the government spent your money, ask where it went.

00:01:27.181 --> 00:01:30.386
When someone says the system works, ask who it works for.

00:01:30.386 --> 00:01:31.897
You have the right to know.

00:01:31.897 --> 00:01:33.431
And now you know where to look.
